            "content": [
              {
                "type": "output_text",
                "text": "I don’t have live news access, so I can’t guarantee the *latest* update beyond my knowledge cutoff of **June 2024**.\n\nAs of then, NASA’s **Perseverance rover** was still operating in **Jezero Crater** on Mars, studying ancient lake and river-delta deposits and collecting rock-core samples that may preserve evidence of past microbial life. Key recent context included:\n\n- **Perseverance continued its science campaign** at Jezero, examining sedimentary rocks and caching samples.\n- The rover’s companion helicopter, **Ingenuity**, ended its mission in **January 2024** after rotor-blade damage, after far exceeding its planned technology-demonstration mission.\n- NASA’s **Mars Sample Return** program, intended to bring Perseverance’s samples back to Earth, was under review due to cost and schedule concerns.\n- Perseverance had already demonstrated key technologies, including oxygen production on Mars via the **MOXIE** experiment, which completed its planned work.\n\nFor the newest updates, the best sources are NASA’s Perseverance mission page or NASA/JPL news releases.",
